    },
    "body": "Hey @quickstar, thanks for the PR! It looks like you hit every point on the new module checklist (I still struggle with that myself, the list is just so long...),so thanks for that.\r\n\r\nThe biggest blocker for me right now is that this module panics all of starship if I just disable all my network interfaces (in that case, I suspect the underlying OS calls fail, since there's no way to actually connect to anything). I think we should fix that and make sure that the warnings aren't too verbose when working offline (should only be a few lines of changes).\r\n\r\nQuick question, since I'm not really a networks person: is there any possibility that someone would ever want to extend this to display IPv6 addresses? If so, would it be better to name the current variable `localipv4` and leave extension for ipv6, or is the convention to use no-suffix to mean v4?",
    "state": "CHANGES_REQUESTED",
